  "work": {
    "description": {
      "type": "/type/text",
      "value": "Airframe is a novel by the American writer Michael Crichton, his eleventh under his own name and twenty-first overall, first published in 1996, in hardcover, by Knopf and then in 1997, as a paperback, by Ballantine Books. The plot follows Casey Singleton, a quality assurance vice president at the fictional aerospace manufacturer Norton Aircraft, as she investigates an in-flight accident aboard a Norton-manufactured airliner that leaves three passengers dead and 56 injured.\r\n\r\n\r\n----------\r\n\r\n\r\nSee also:\r\n[Airframe. 1/2](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28764897W/Airframe._1_2)"
    },
